llback's error raised in f"] [86 5 "// a jump (f_lineno) from the yield's event: the frame goes on there, the value not yielded"] [87 5 "// (INSTRUMENTED_YIELD_VALUE's frame->instr_ptr check; queue 281: test_sys_settrace's test_jump_from_yield)"] [93 4 "// f returned v"] [101 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [109 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [122 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [137 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee; then"] [138 5 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START (queue 220: breakMonitor keeps the breaker set while a tool has events)"] [149 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [155 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [160 40 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [161 40 "// RERAISE (queue 281: monitor_reraise)"] [169 41 "// END_ASYNC_FOR's RERAISE (queue 281)"] [172 45 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [177 43 "// EXCEPTION_HANDLED (queue 281: monitor_handled)"] [187 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [193 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [195 6 "// the handler CPython wraps a generator's body in (codegen's STOPITERATION_ERROR and RERAISE; queue 281)"] [211 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [212 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [213 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [216 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [217 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [220 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [228 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [231 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [232 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [233 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [234 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [236 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [248 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [260 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [261 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [269 25 "// a generator argument left suspended (queue 297): checked by the caller (callDropped)"] [282 24 "// a generator argument left suspended (queue 297): checked by the caller (callDropped)"] [298 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [305 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [306 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [307 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [310 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [311 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [312 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by run